@format 1
@id tabs.move
@title Move tab
@area UI workflow
@entry input
@summary Reorder one tab with a pointer-following ghost, then keep it in this window or relay it on release.
@section I. UI
@tabs Global interface
@flow TB
@related tabs.select, tabs.relay-out

@alias navigator = Cadroue.UIShell.PControlBar.PTabNavigator
@alias tabset = Cadroue.UIShell.PControlBar.LTabset
@alias ghost = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainWindow.PGhost

[input] Tab drag begins <input>
- Store the pressed tab, source element, drag origin, and pointer grab offset @ navigator.PTabPressHandle(...)
- Select the tab and capture the mouse to its visual element @ navigator.PTabPressHandle(...)
> threshold

[threshold] Drag threshold crossed? <decision>
- Compare pointer travel with the standard horizontal and vertical drag distances @ navigator.PTabMoveHandle(...)
? "No" > waiting
? "Yes" > visualize

[visualize] Show drag feedback <process>
- Dim the live tab and capture its rendered image in an adorner-layer ghost @ ghost.PGhostShow(...)
> track

[track] Track pointer and insertion <process>
- Synchronize the ghost with the system cursor @ ghost.PGhostCursorSync(...)
- Resolve the insertion index from tab centers @ navigator.PTabIndexResolve(...)
- Immediately move the real tab record to the resolved index @ tabset.LTabsetMove(...)
> release

[release] Finish drag <decision>
- Restore the tab opacity, remove the ghost, and release mouse capture @ navigator.PTabDragClear(...)
- Check whether the release point is outside the current window @ navigator.PTabRelayCheck(...)
? "Inside this window or relay fails" > result
? "Relay succeeds" > relayed

[result] Tab moved <output>
= The tab remains in this window at its latest resolved index.

[relayed] Tab relayed <output>
= The destination receives the tab and the source tab closes.

[waiting] Click remains below threshold <output>
= No ghost is created and tab order does not change.
